Falsifies `usb::verification::the_header_parsers_are_total`.

The defect: `DeviceDescriptor::parse` loses its length check and indexes `b[0]` of whatever it is handed, so an
empty or short descriptor from the device is an out-of-bounds read.

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `b[0]` in `DeviceDescriptor::parse`.

diff --git a/crates/usb/src/descriptor.rs b/crates/usb/src/descriptor.rs
index cb5c8bef7..857bc3010 100644
--- a/crates/usb/src/descriptor.rs
+++ b/crates/usb/src/descriptor.rs
@@ -88,3 +88,3 @@ impl DeviceDescriptor {
     pub fn parse(b: &[u8]) -> Option<DeviceDescriptor> {
-        if b.len() < DEVICE_LEN || (b[0] as usize) < DEVICE_LEN || b[1] != DEVICE {
+        if (b[0] as usize) < DEVICE_LEN || b[1] != DEVICE {
             return None;
